# Scroll fade

Figma reference: `# design` fades outside system UI
(`O7SlK5o3Ozt8ztG4Ds8iZY` node `2749:8352`) — `top-fade` / `bottom-fade`
(`top-scroll` / `bottom-scroll` gradients).

## System-UI placement (Work Out / full-bleed scroll)

Fades sit **inside** the safe area, not under the status bar or home indicator:

| Edge | Figma | Code |
|------|-------|------|
| Top | `top: 62` (below status bar), height `s-17` | `topOffset={insets.top}`, `topFadeHeight={spacing['s-17']}` |
| Bottom | `bottom: 34` (above home indicator), height `s-16` | `bottomOffset={insets.bottom}`, `bottomFadeHeight={SCROLL_FADE_HEIGHT}` |

Do **not** pin fades to app chrome (title / footer buttons). System insets only.

When `topOffset` / `bottomOffset` are set, `ScrollFadeView` also paints a solid
`bg-1` cap in the inset band so scrolled content cannot show through the status
bar or home-indicator region (the gradient alone starts *after* the inset and
would leave that band uncovered).

## When

Use `ScrollFadeView` instead of bare `ScrollView` when content can scroll vertically inside a fixed viewport.

## How

```tsx
import { ScrollFadeView } from '../components/ScrollFadeView';

<ScrollFadeView
  contentContainerStyle={styles.content}
  showsVerticalScrollIndicator={false}
  style={styles.scroll}
>
  {children}
</ScrollFadeView>

// Work Out — outside system UI (Figma # design)
<ScrollFadeView
  topFadeHeight={spacing['s-17']}
  bottomFadeHeight={SCROLL_FADE_HEIGHT}
  topOffset={insets.top}
  bottomOffset={insets.bottom}
  ...
>
```

- Tokens and visibility rules: `src/theme/scrollFade.ts` (`SCROLL_FADE_HEIGHT`, `scrollFadeGradients`, `getScrollFadeVisibility`)
- Component: `src/components/ScrollFadeView.tsx`
- Default fade height: `spacing['s-16']` via `fadeHeight`, or per-edge overrides
- Gradients: `bg-1` ↔ `content-trans-dark` — import from `scrollFade.ts`, never duplicate inline
- Show/hide: opacity animates (~250ms) when edges enter or leave; fades stay mounted while content overflows

## Overrides

Only tune via props when layout requires it:

| Prop | Use |
|------|-----|
| `fadeHeight` | Shared default height for both fades when top/bottom heights are omitted |
| `topFadeHeight` | Top band only — overrides `fadeHeight` |
| `bottomFadeHeight` | Bottom band only — overrides `fadeHeight` |
| `topOffset` | Push top fade below system status inset (`insets.top`) |
| `bottomOffset` | Push bottom fade above home-indicator inset (`insets.bottom`) |
| `topFadeEnabled` | Set `false` when pinned chrome replaces the top fade (e.g. Settings title bar) |

## Layering

- Fades live **inside** the scroll viewport (`ScrollFadeView` container), `pointerEvents: none`
- Pinned chrome (title bars, CTAs, pinned footers, bottom sheets) stays **outside** and above the fade layer

## FlatList / SectionList

No wrapper yet. Use `getScrollFadeVisibility` + manual `LinearGradient` overlays, or add a `ScrollFadeHost` follow-up.
